{#- PatchMon agent (formulas/patchmon is the server). A static Go binary
   from the GitHub release, pinned by version + sha256 — no container, so
   it also runs on salt-master/wazuh without Docker. Bump together with the
   server tag (README "Upgrades"); Renovate doesn't see this pin.

   server_url: where the agent connects (http + WebSocket).
   enroll_key / enroll_secret: one PatchMon auto-enrollment token for all  (secret-scan: allow)
   minions (README "Enrolment"), from OpenBao via pillar. A minion without
   credentials.yml enrols itself with it (friendly name = minion ID) and
   keeps the per-host credentials it gets back; the token file is deleted
   after that. No credentials and no token (empty/unresolved) = binary only,
   no service, no failure — a clean highstate either way.

   config.yml belongs to the agent after the first write: it rewrites
   update_interval, integrations, host_id itself. Salt creates it once and
   afterwards only enforces patchmon_server and ssh/rdp proxy = false
   (`enforce`). #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'version': '2.1.8',
    'sha256': '6c143ec193153513f677b0b114f52aa0b6bf2554c95f407a016e3d20d9ad680c',
    'url': 'https://github.com/PatchMon/PatchMon/releases/download/v{version}/patchmon-agent-linux-amd64',
    'bin': '/usr/local/bin/patchmon-agent',
    'config_dir': '/etc/patchmon',
    'unit': 'patchmon-agent',
    'server_url': '',
    'enroll_key': '',
    'enroll_secret': '',
    'enroll_script': '/usr/local/sbin/patchmon-agent-enroll',
    'log_level': 'info',
} %}
{%- set agent = salt['pillar.get']('patchmon-agent:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
{%- set _k = agent.enroll_key or '' %}
{%- set _s = agent.enroll_secret or '' %}
{%- set token_ok = (_k and _s and agent.server_url
                    and not _k.startswith('sdb://') and not _s.startswith('sdb://')) and true or false %}
{%- set creds_file = agent.config_dir ~ '/credentials.yml' %}
{%- set has_creds = salt['file.file_exists'](creds_file) %}
{%- do agent.update({
      'creds_file': creds_file,
      'token_file': agent.config_dir ~ '/enroll-token.json',
      'enroll': token_ok and not has_creds,
      'enrolled': has_creds or token_ok,
    }) %}
